// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`security.habitat.redteam given: [case1] the guardian role installed via rhachet init when: [t1] the human asks for help then: it names every command and grain (exit 0) 1`] = `
"🐈 heres the deal...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam — hunt a habitat the way an adversary would

   the ward loop: ground → detect → verify → repair → promote → (loop | terminate)

usage:
  rhx security.habitat.redteam init --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] [--skip-route-bind]
  rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] --mode plan
  rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] [--skip-route-bind] --mode apply

ward-loop gates (the stones invoke these; never the raw command they guard):
  rhx security.habitat.redteam backup-before-rewrite                     (4.repair, before each history rewrite)
  printf '%s' "$body" | rhx security.habitat.redteam dispatch-lesson --title <title>
  rhx security.habitat.redteam rewind-detect --route <route> --cycle <n> <<'KEYS'
  <each open key, one per line, written out in full>
  KEYS

options:
  --scope            habitat surface to sweep (a repo, a subtree)         (required)
  --grain            infil | exfil | leak | all                           (required)
                     infil = what reaches in · exfil = what can leave, by any outbound channel · leak = what your own next push publishes · all = the three
  --peers            blind peers per grain-partition, 1 to 9999           (default: 3; apply to a bound route: its own; fixed once 1.ground cuts the slices)
  --budget           loop spend allowance, 1 to 9999 cycles               (default: 1 — one pass, no re-detect; apply to a bound route: its own)
  --mode             plan | apply                                         (required, except for init)
  --skip-route-bind  scaffold without a branch bind                       (apply + init only)

gate options (each gate reads only its own; any other flag belays):
  --title            dispatch-lesson: the lesson's title, '<class>: <fix>' (required)
  --route            rewind-detect: the route dir under .behavior/        (required)
  --cycle            rewind-detect: the cycle just walked, 1 to 9999      (required)

exit: 0 = done · 1 = malfunction · 2 = constraint

⚠️ informational only — not professional security advice, not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for your own habitat
"
`;

exports[`security.habitat.redteam given: [case1] the guardian role installed via rhachet init when: [t2] the human plans a sweep then: it names the spend and the outward acts, and stops (exit 0) 1`] = `
"🐈 chartin course...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam --mode plan --scope . --grain leak --peers 3 --budget 1
   ├─ scope: .
   ├─ grains: leak  (1 grain-partition, disjoint by grain-surface)
   ├─ peers: 3 per grain-partition  ⇒ 3 blind peers total
   ├─ budget: 1 loop cycle — each draws one detect → verify → repair pass
   ├─ re-detect: none — one pass; its repairs stay PENDING-REDETECT and cannot converge (pass --budget 2 or more to re-detect them)
   ├─ projected: 3 peers × 1 cycle = up to 3 peer-dispatch runs
   ├─ a bound route: apply keeps its recorded peers + budget for any flag this request omits; a new --peers is refused once 1.ground cuts the slices
   ├─ the ward loop: ground → detect → verify → repair → promote → (loop | terminate)
   ├─ publishes: 5.promote opens a public gh issue on ehmpathy/rhachet-roles-ghlitch per fullsun-safe lesson (a generalized class, never a live claim); each push runs the dispatch-lesson scan gate first, and live claims stay in .claims/
   ├─ defers: 4.repair never revokes or rotates a credential at its issuer — it drafts the command for a human to run, and the claim stays open until the human returns its output
   ├─ rewrites: 4.repair edits the tree and rewrites each local unpushed commit that carries a leaked value — each rewrite passes rhx security.habitat.redteam backup-before-rewrite first, which takes a backup ref (refs/redteam-backup/<branch>.<head-sha>, never pushed by --all) and refuses the rewrite when the tree holds uncommitted work
   ├─ per-peer slices: 3 per grain-partition, cut by 1.ground at drive time into .claims/1.ground.yield.md — its guard grades them, and the drive goes on to 2.detect with no pause; this plan is your read before the spend
   ├─ scope limit: blind peers cannot see the aggregate map (a leak only the whole published set forms); a clean verdict does not clear it — review the whole corpus for that class apart
   ├─ per-grain prompts (each peer is blind to the others' slice + theory)
   │  ├─ leak  — "what value on this slice is already exposed, or forms a map with others?"
   │  └─ each claim = a chain (entry/exit → mechanism → blast radius|audience), keyed on channel+mechanism
   └─ next: spend it: rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope . --grain leak --peers 3 --budget 1 --mode apply

⚠️ informational only — not professional security advice, not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for your own habitat
"
`;

